description:
Repair every case where selected-option behavior is absent, hoisted to a parent
record, or flattened into an unconditional array.

Root cause: options and variants have no semantic ownership of their own, so
their effects are attached to the parent feature or emitted as a flat list.

Required membership — all of:
- fighting styles, Hunter option sets, Eldritch Invocations, metamagic, pact
  boons;
- ASI one-score/two-score allocation and repeated improvements;
- language choices, including the campaign/GM extension escape hatch;
- ability alternatives and mutually exclusive damage modes;
- pit variants and other source-defined variants;
- stable typed option identifiers and prerequisites.

Closes findings: SOL-002, SOL-011, F-02, F-07, F-14, F-27, F-33, F-35, CAP-005.
